{"id":"56c2fd81-5b12-4d71-af16-0a0a111f9aa2","object":"chat.completion","created":1785028267,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    # Validate required fields\\n    if 'nodes' not in case or 'required_symbols' not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Missing required fields: nodes and required_symbols\\\")\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    required_symbols = case['required_symbols']\\n    if not isinstance(nodes, list) or not isinstance(required_symbols, list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"nodes must be a list, required_symbols must be a list\\\")\\n    # Build map id->node\\n    node_map = {}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        if 'id' not in n or 'parent' not in n or 'symbol' not in n or 'depth' not in n or 'removable' not in n or 'utility' not in n:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"Each node must have id, parent, symbol, depth, removable, utility\\\")\\n        node_map[n['id']] = n\\n    # Check required symbols exist at least once\\n    symbol_present = {n['symbol'] for n in nodes}\\n    for s in required_symbols:\\n        if s not in symbol_present:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Required symbol {s} not present in tree\\\")\\n    # Find root(s)\\n    roots = [n['id'] for n in nodes if n['parent'] is None]\\n    if len(roots) != 1:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Tree must have exactly one root\\\")\\n    root_id = roots[0]\\n    # Build children adjacency\\n    children = {n['id']: [] for n in nodes}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        p = n['parent']\\n        if p is not None:\\n            if p not in node_map:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"Parent {p} not found\\\")\\n            children[p].append(n['id'])\\n    # Mark required nodes: root and any node whose symbol is in required_symbols\\n    cannot_remove = {root_id}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        if n['symbol'] in required_symbols:\\n            cannot_remove.add(n['id'])\\n    # Sort candidates by descending depth, then ascending id\\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n['depth'], n['id']))\\n    removed = set()\\n    removal_order = []\\n    for n in sorted_nodes:\\n        nid = n['id']\\n        if nid in cannot_remove or not n['removable']:\\n            continue\\n        # Check that all children are already removed (i.e., no retained children)\\n        if any(child_id not in removed for child_id in children[nid]):\\n            continue\\n        # Additional check: required symbols remain represented.\\n        # Since node's own symbol is not required (already in cannot_remove) and all children are removed,\\n        # no required symbols are lost, so condition is automatically satisfied.\\n        removal_order.append(nid)\\n        removed.add(nid)\\n    # Build retained IDs sorted\\n    retained_ids = sorted([n['id'] for n in nodes if n['id'] not in removed])\\n    return {\\n        \\\"removed_node_ids\\\": removal_order,\\n        \\\"retained_node_ids\\\": retained_ids\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement solve(case) based on the description. The task: grammar_guided_node_reduction (SE-PE-01). The input case has nodes list and required_symbols. Nodes have id, parent, symbol, depth, removable, utility. We need to determine which nodes to remove and which to retain, following rules:\n\n- Never remove the root (id \"root\"? but check parent null). \n- Never remove a required symbol node? Actually \"Never remove a required symbol\" means nodes whose symbol is in required_symbols? Or nodes that represent required symbols? Probably nodes whose symbol is in required_symbols are not removable. But note that some nodes have removable flag. But according to description: \"Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children.\" So nodes with symbol in required_symbols should not be removed, regardless of removable flag? Also \"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented.\" That means before removing a node, we must check that after removal, all required symbols are still present in the tree (from retained nodes). Also we need to consider deeper nodes before shallower nodes (i.e., process nodes in descending depth order, deeper first). At equal depth, use node ID as tie break (stable). \n\nWe need to decide removal order. The output requires removed_node_ids (order of removal) and retained_node_ids (sorted IDs). \n\nWe need to implement algorithm:\n\n- Build tree structure from nodes list.\n- Identify root (parent null). \n- Identify nodes that are \"required\" based on symbol in required_symbols. They cannot be removed.\n- Also nodes marked removable=False? Actually description says \"Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children.\" The removable flag might be additional constraint? The task says \"Treat these registered properties as hard contracts: grammar_valid, interestingness_preserved, registered_candidate_order, stable_ties.\" The removable flag might be part of \"grammar_valid\" or \"registered_candidate_order\"? But looking at the fixture, some nodes have removable: true, some false. The rule \"Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children.\" So if a node has removable false but is not root/required/with children, can we remove it? Probably not, because removable false indicates it's not a candidate for removal. So we should only consider nodes with removable == true as candidates. The description says \"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented.\" So candidates are those where removable is true, and not root, not required symbol, and has no retained children (i.e., children that will be retained? Actually \"node with retained children\" - if we are planning to remove a node, we must ensure that no children are retained (i.e., we would also remove its children). But we process deeper nodes first, so children are considered